<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 81,868 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 81,868 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 81,868 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday, compared to 40,532 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Friday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 8,440	     6,148</p>
<p>    Import cargo			73,428	    27,932</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Mogas		    25,000	 Athenian Success    due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     31/5</p>
<p>Gas oil		  78,000	 Chesapeak City     28/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 26,000	 Zoras		   due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Ying Song Hu	 31/5</p>
<p>Crude oil		60,000	 Capitan Miranda     due</p>
<p>Vegoil		   18,000	 Ariston		28/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
